W AX3051 378-restrict-no-cast-deep.ax:68:6-17 restriction-unverifiable "`deepPartial` claims `restrict(no-cast:deep)` and the claim cannot be checked: the body calls a value the compiler could not resolve, so its closure cannot be enumerated" ?"a limit of the ANALYSIS rather than a defect in the program - AX3037's argument at one remove. There are four readings: an effect present only as POSSIBLE, a row the walk marked incomplete, a body that CALLS one of its own parameters (`#effect-params=`), whose answer is chosen by each caller and cannot be settled here at all, and - for `no-escape` alone - a region fixpoint that hit its round limit before the facts settled, which is a depth limit rather than anything about this declaration. Name the function at the call, stop calling the parameter, shorten the chain, or drop the claim; `no-cast`, `no-wrap` and `no-trap` are checked regardless, because all three are lexical and need no call resolved"
E AX3073 378-restrict-no-cast-deep.ax:30:4-6 undeclared-unsafe "`unwrap` erases `Meters` into `Int` with `as`, and its declaration does not say so" #"erases a reference" ^30:7-8:"source has type `Meters`; the conversion drops its ownership" ?29:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"keep the value in a typed binding, or use `addrOf` when the question is identity. An erasing cast drops the type and the share" ?"the unsafe tag marks a trusted boundary: you must make every well-typed call safe. It leaves ordinary type, effect and restriction checks in place"
E AX3049 378-restrict-no-cast-deep.ax:38:6-16 restriction-violated "`deepCaller` claims `restrict(no-cast:deep)` and the closure reaches a cast in the body of `unwrap`: deepCaller -> unwrap" ^29:6-12:"unwrap" ?"a restriction is a CLAIM the author wrote, and this is the compiler answering it. `no-io`, `no-alloc`, `no-unsafe`, `no-foreign`, `no-cast:deep` and `no-recursion` are transitive - the effect row and the call graph are fixpoints over every callee - and the path in the message is the chain of resolved calls (`symbols --calls` spells each hop the same way) from this declaration to where the effect enters, or around the cycle, so the fix is at a named place rather than somewhere below. Make the body keep the claim, or delete the tag, which WITHDRAWS the claim rather than answering it; an unrestricted function is never asked"
E AX3049 378-restrict-no-cast-deep.ax:43:6-13 restriction-violated "`deepFar` claims `restrict(no-cast:deep)` and the closure reaches a cast in the body of `unwrap`: deepFar -> viaUnwrap -> unwrap" ^33:6-15:"viaUnwrap" ^29:6-12:"unwrap" ?"a restriction is a CLAIM the author wrote, and this is the compiler answering it. `no-io`, `no-alloc`, `no-unsafe`, `no-foreign`, `no-cast:deep` and `no-recursion` are transitive - the effect row and the call graph are fixpoints over every callee - and the path in the message is the chain of resolved calls (`symbols --calls` spells each hop the same way) from this declaration to where the effect enters, or around the cycle, so the fix is at a named place rather than somewhere below. Make the body keep the claim, or delete the tag, which WITHDRAWS the claim rather than answering it; an unrestricted function is never asked"
E AX3049 378-restrict-no-cast-deep.ax:49:7-9 restriction-violated "`as` in the body of `deepLocal`, which claims `restrict(no-cast:deep)`" ?"`no-cast` rejects explicit conversions in this body. Use an operation that preserves the required type, or remove the restriction. `no-cast:deep` also follows resolved callees; an unresolved path cannot establish the claim."
